      "text": "Step 1: To find the maximum value of \\( f(x, y) = x \\sqrt{1 - y^2} + y \\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\), we can use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality in the form \\((a_1b_1 + a_2b_2)^2 \\leq (a_1^2 + a_2^2)(b_1^2 + b_2^2)\\).",
